From 87c471ce9a7a0ded092d9413b5e6e35c6c3ba2b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:51:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtime): decode a 4:2:2 texture over a buffer into a
 twin its samples read

Local (Asahi/Honeykrisp). A GBGR422 or BGRG422 texture over a buffer's
bytes (an IOSurface plane of a CoreVideo 2vuy or yuvs surface, a
software decoder's frame) had no decoded twin, so a binding that sampled
it was refused for want of SAMPLED on its carrier, and VideoToolbox's
pixel-transfer kernel could not read a ProRes frame.

Such a texture is now always a shadow with a decoded twin
(Device::with_surface_twin). The bytes are written by the CPU with no
call the runtime sees, so the twin is decoded on the CPU from the
buffer's bytes as each sampled view of the texture is bound, unless they
are the pairs it was last decoded from (Texture::refresh_surface_twin),
and copied into the twin on the host or the staging queue. A detach
keeps the twin's texels and presents the carrier's stand-in.
